+# Threshold Feature Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+Added threshold validation support to `frai eval` to gate CI jobs on evaluation metrics.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. CLI Layer (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`)
+
+#### EvalOptions Interface
+- Added `threshold?: string[]` field to support multiple threshold arguments
+
+#### parseThresholds Function
+- Parses `--threshold` arguments in format `metric=value`
+- Validates metric names against list: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+- Validates values are numbers between 0 and 1
+- Returns `Record<string, number> | null`
+- Exits with code 2 on validation errors with descriptive messages
+
+#### eval Command Definition
+- Added `--threshold <metric=value>` option (repeatable)
+- Handler extracts and normalizes threshold array from options
+
+#### runEvalCommand Function
+- Calls `parseThresholds()` to validate user input
+- Passes validated thresholds to `generateReport()` via spread operator
+- Exits with code 1 if `report.passed === false`
+
+### 2. Core Logic (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)
+
+#### generateReport Function
+- Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter: `Record<string, number>`
+- Evaluates each threshold against metric evaluations:
+  - Finds metric by id
+  - Checks if `metric.score >= minScore`
+  - Treats null scores as failed thresholds
+- Builds `thresholdResults` array with structure:
+  ```js
+  {
+    metric: string,      // metric id
+    min: number,         // threshold minimum
+    score: number|null,  // actual metric score
+    passed: boolean      // whether threshold passed
+  }
+  ```
+- Adds `passed` boolean (true if all thresholds pass) to report
+- Adds `thresholds` array to report only when thresholds are specified
+
+### 3. Output Formatters (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)
+
+#### toMarkdown Function
+- Added "## Thresholds" section (displays only if thresholds exist)
+- Shows each threshold with format:
+  ```
+  - **metric_id:** ✓ PASS (score: X.XXXX, min: Y.YYYY)
+  - **metric_id:** ✗ FAIL (score: null, min: Y.YYYY)
+  ```
+
+#### toJson Function
+- No changes needed - JSON serialization automatically includes new fields
+
+### 4. Tests (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`)
+
+Added 4 new test cases:
+1. **evaluates thresholds - all pass** - validates passed flag and threshold structure
+2. **evaluates thresholds - some fail** - validates failed thresholds set passed to false
+3. **handles thresholds with missing metric scores** - validates null scores fail
+4. **writes markdown report with thresholds section** - validates markdown output format
+
+### 5. Documentation
+
+#### README.md
+- Updated `frai eval` CLI options to document `--threshold` parameter
+- Added valid metrics list and value range constraints
+- Added SDK example showing how to use thresholds programmatically
+
+#### docs/eval_harness_design.md
+- Updated MVP Scope to mention threshold validation feature
+- Noted exit codes for failure and usage errors
+
+## Behavior
+
+### Without Thresholds
+- Behavior unchanged from previous version
+- Reports generated as before
+- Exit code always 0
+
+### With Thresholds
+- **All pass:** exit code 0, `report.passed = true`
+- **Some fail:** exit code 1, `report.passed = false`
+- **Invalid format/metric:** exit code 2, error message logged, no report written
+
+### Report Structure with Thresholds
+
+JSON:
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [ ... ],
+  "passed": true,
+  "thresholds": [
+    { "metric": "exact_match", "min": 0.9, "score": 0.95, "passed": true },
+    { "metric": "toxicity", "min": 0.5, "score": 1.0, "passed": true }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Markdown:
+```markdown
+## Thresholds
+
+- **exact_match:** ✓ PASS (score: 0.95, min: 0.9)
+- **toxicity:** ✓ PASS (score: 1.0, min: 0.5)
+
+## Metrics
+...
+```
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### CLI
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.5
+
+# In CI with exit code checking
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --format json || echo "Thresholds failed"
+```
+
+### SDK
+```javascript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({ outputs, references });
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'refs.json',
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.5 }
+});
+
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('Thresholds failed!');
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+- Custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()` automatically work with thresholds as long as they have `id` and `score` fields
+- Threshold validation happens before report generation, so invalid thresholds don't produce partial reports
+- The feature is fully backwards compatible - existing code without thresholds works unchanged
